<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Yankee Team, 1966</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;----------------------------------------------------&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;FONT face=Gisha&gt;&lt;FONT size=6 face="Trebuchet MS"&gt;Yankee Team&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;---------------------------------------------------&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;EM&gt;Carrier Air Ops vs. North Vietnam, 1966&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=3&gt;---------------------------------------------------&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;IMG style="HEIGHT: 317px; WIDTH: 423px" alt=http://i.imgur.com/bPWFXlE.jpg src="http://i.imgur.com/bPWFXlE.jpg" width=498 height=398&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;FONT size=1&gt;Scenario by George Ross, v1.50&lt;BR&gt;(For CMANO v1.12 + Chains of War DLC)&lt;BR&gt;------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;BR&gt;Users without CoW can download version 1.30 here: &lt;A href="https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B77YKog18qtvbGdENzA2UFBTdEU"&gt;https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B77YKog18qtvbGdENzA2UFBTdEU&lt;/A&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;BR&gt;Dynamic Mission,&lt;/STRONG&gt; 24 hours, Forces: 190-225 total aircraft &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;(~3/4 will&amp;nbsp;available for sorties)&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;NOTE:&lt;/STRONG&gt; Make sure to enable 'Special Messages' as&amp;nbsp;pop-ups for the message log in the game settings - many important instructions in this scenario rely on them.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=left&gt;Welcome to the Gulf of Tonkin Yacht Club, &lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;FONT size=3&gt;commander!&lt;/FONT&gt; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=left&gt;Operation Rolling Thunder continues apace for the Navy. For the next 24 hours, you will be overseeing air operations for Task Force 77, on station at Yankee Point and conducting strikes on North Vietnam. The targets for today, located in the USN's area of air operations at Route Packages 2, 3, 4 and 6B, have&amp;nbsp;just been assigned with direct oversight from the White House.&amp;nbsp;It is sure to be a long day.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=left&gt;This is a dynamic mission which makes extensive use of Command's event scripting features - your strike force and starting conditions, your targets,&amp;nbsp;and your enemy's SAM defenses &lt;EM&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;(and to a lesser extent MiG patrols)&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/EM&gt; are generated when you start the scenario, and are sure to create a different experience every time you play. Rather than accurately recreating any specific action, this mission is meant to put you in the shoes of the air commander, always facing some uncertainty and risk. Your task force of 3 carriers will be picked from a combination of a total&amp;nbsp;9 ships, each with a historically-accurate squadron roster from mid-late 1966.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;You will command the air groups of&amp;nbsp;the carriers (though not the carriers themselves), which are doing their turns in the strike&amp;nbsp;line at Yankee Station today. The first is already on station for its 12-hour shift, while the other two will arrive for theirs 6 and 12 hours from now. You'll be choosing the targets, arming the planes, and sending them into the North. &lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;Good luck!&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;(This scenario will play differently each time - try it more than once if you like it.)&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
  <Complexity>4</Complexity>
  <Difficulty>3</Difficulty>
  <ScenSetting>Vietnam</ScenSetting>
  <ScenDate>1966</ScenDate>
